If I were to organize such a dinner party with no specific host constraints, I would love to have:

1. Confucius - for his profound philosophical insights and thoughts on humanity;
2. Emperor Qin Shi Huang - to learn about the grand and fascinating history of China;
3. Some brilliant individuals from ancient Chinese literature or calligraphy, such as Wang Xizhi (but note that I cannot specify which figures, as this would be a more complex task);
4. The great Tang Dynasty poets, like Li Bai or Du Fu, to appreciate the beauty and grace of classical Chinese poetry;

Instead of sticking to historical figures, I'd prefer to mention some truly remarkable scientific figures or individuals who made significant contributions to society, such as Sun Simiao or Lu Yu, as well as the likes of Zu Chongzhi.

Certainly, if the goal was to simply honor ancient Chinese culture with someone not named above or a figure that had already contributed in a particular field, I would want to invite

